Package: wayland-headless-harness
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Stuart Axon <stuaxo2@yahoo.com>
Depends: bash, psmisc, iproute2, podman, sudo, python3, python3-typer, python3-click, python3-rich
Section: net
Priority: optional
Description: Headless multi-compositor Wayland test harness
 Spins up headless, containerized instances of labwc, sway, kwin, and
 gnome-shell (mutter) for reproducing Wayland client/compositor
 protocol issues across real compositor implementations, without
 needing a full desktop session on the host.
 .
 Includes crash/reconnect testing tooling for an optional proxy under
 test (e.g. wayland-proxy) -- the container matrix and diagnostics work
 standalone too, with no proxy involved, for straightforward
 compositor/client debugging.
